# Implement a generic configurable Rust algorithm creator and replayer

Replace research-specific reconstruction generators with one source-agnostic
Rust foundation function that records deterministic, source-bound reconstruction
algorithms as durable `.txt` data and replays them only from admitted local
source evidence.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Own the implementation at `src/foundation/algorithm/` as a Rust workspace
  crate with no game-, icon-, Doom-, or Malbolge-specific behavior.
- [x] Load generic authoring controls from
  `src/foundation/algorithm/composition/adapter-inbound/settings.json`; settings
  define mechanism limits and
  defaults, never product-specific source identities or similarity policy.
- [x] Provide a small CLI that accepts one or more source files or directories,
  a target file or directory to record, and an explicit output path whose file
  name ends in `.txt`.
- [x] Provide deterministic replay from the `.txt` algorithm plus caller-supplied
  source files/directories into an explicit output path.
- [x] Canonicalize and sort input trees, reject redirects/special entries, reject
  duplicate portable paths, and never write inside source inputs.
- [x] Bind protected target literals to source evidence so the public algorithm
  does not contain target files as plaintext or as a source-independent
  reversible payload.
- [x] Authenticate protected payloads and fail closed on altered algorithms,
  wrong source evidence, path traversal, output collisions, or target hash
  mismatch.
- [x] Reuse shared SHAR foundation crates for filesystem and SHA-256 behavior
  instead of duplicating repository mechanisms.
- [x] Cover deterministic author/replay, file and directory inputs, wrong-source
  rejection, tamper rejection, path safety, `.txt` output validation, and
  settings validation with Rust tests.
- [x] Delete
  `src/foundation/algorithm/reference-delete-this-after-implementation/` only
  after useful generic behavior has been implemented and the icon exporter has
  been preserved in its final migration boundary.

## Security and policy boundary

This crate owns mechanics, not SHAR release-admission policy. In particular it
must not hard-code the tentative public reconstruction similarity window. The
separate similarity-gate TODO remains responsible for representative lawful
calibration and final distributable admission thresholds.

The protected representation may contain ciphertext and authenticated metadata,
but lawful source evidence must remain materially necessary to recover protected
target literals. The recorded format must therefore never store target files as
bare base64, bare hex, compression, XOR with a public constant, or another
source-independent reversible encoding. Text-encoding authenticated ciphertext is
allowed because the source-derived key remains necessary for recovery.

## Evidence

`11c72492` introduced the `src/foundation/algorithm/` Rust workspace crate, its
mechanism-only `settings.json`, the `algorithm create|replay` CLI, deterministic
JSON `.txt` serialization, SHA-256 source identities, and ChaCha20-Poly1305
protected target payloads. The engine derives its payload key from the admitted
source bytes, authenticates static source/target metadata as associated data,
checks recovered target identities, and decrypts the complete plan before any
replay output is published.

`070f172a` added shared fail-closed filesystem traversal and switched algorithm
source/target directory collection to it. Redirects and special entries are
rejected while portable-path collision validation remains centralized in the
filesystem foundation. `bf75f784` and `87f3f4fe` expanded Rust coverage for
source overlap, parent traversal, redirected trees, altered target paths,
existing-output collisions, target-hash tampering, wrong sources, authenticated
payload tampering, `.txt` enforcement, settings validation, file targets,
directory targets, and deterministic byte-identical authoring.

The crate contains no game, icon, Doom, Malbolge, or similarity-window policy.
The imported reference directory has been removed. Its useful icon exporter was
preserved separately under `src/migration/icon/`, and `8c6d8878` published the
source-bound `icon_algorithm.txt` without publishing the ignored local SVG
oracle or generated platform outputs.
